    "created_at": "2023-08-01T09:26:29Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-08-01T09:26:29Z",
    "body": "Having static and dynamic imports diverge makes perfect sense! The former is part of the initialization, initiated by the outside, and is done before the worker even exists (in some implementations, before the thread has even been spun up or the global object allocated). The latter is initiated by the inside, after initialization.\r\n\r\nIn general, the outer page is initiating the initial graph fetch, and its CSP and security policies should apply. The inner worker is initiating dynamic imports, and so *its* security policies should apply.\r\n\r\nTrying to say that the worker code initiated the static imports seems incorrect, in that sense. It's the outer page that kicked it off.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/1659926757/reactions",
      "total_count": 0,
      "+1": 0,
