    "updated_at": "2023-08-17T08:55:31Z",
    "body": "I can see that it may be surprising to some that there's a difference between child fetches in the initial module graph and dynamic imports, but still, I agree with @domenic. Especially this I think is compelling:\r\n\r\n> Indeed, many web developers are used to an isomorphism: bundled code behaves the same as unbundled code.\r\n\r\nAlso, as a data point, `importScripts()` uses the worker's settings object, and AFAIK we haven't heard complaints about it.",
